      ":question/problem": "![](images/c1/c1e3928642960884851434698c3a66edd17ce5b9b65d08dd3f4d3ae7e3317cee.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows a relationship between the stress level scores $(x)$ and the grades $(y)$ (measured in $%$) for students taking an exam. The corresponding best fit quadratic model is given by\n$y =-7x^{2} + 60x - 40$.\nEstimate the grade for a student with a stress level score of $4$ points.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
